<title>NETHERLANDS: Akzo Nobel sells Mexican stake.</title>
<headline>Akzo Nobel sells Mexican stake.</headline>
<dateline>ARNHEM, Netherlands 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemical group Akzo Nobel NV said on Monday it had sold its 40 percent interest in Mexico's Fibras Quimicas to petrochemicals group Alfa which now owns 100 percent of the fibres maker.  </p>
<p>Akzo said Fibras Quimicas aimed at expanding in the segment of polyester textiles and would need substantial investments for this strategy.</p>
<p>&quot;Taking part in these investments would not be in line with Akzo Nobel's policy to focus on leading positions in core activities,&quot; the Dutch firm said in a statement.</p>
<p>It did not disclose any financial details of the sale of the 40 percent stake to Alfa's subsidiary Alpek.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
